      <div id="textid" class="col-sm-12">
  # Theory-guided Interpretation of Actinide Spectroscopy and Electronic Structure

<div style="background:#efeee8; border:1px solid #c9c9c1; padding:30px 35px; margin:25px 0 45px;">

<div style="display:flex; gap:35px; align-items:center;">

<div style="flex:1.7;">

<p style="margin-top:0;">
Our research uses quantum chemistry methods to understand the electronic structure of f-element compounds; these exhibit complex electronic behaviour due to strong electron correlation and relativistic effects, making them among the most challenging systems in chemistry.
</p>

<p>
We develop and apply advanced electronic structure methods to predict spectroscopic properties, understand chemical bonding, and explain magnetic behaviour. Through close collaboration with experimental researchers, we ensure that our theoretical approaches are as close as possible to experimental reality.
</p>

</div>

<div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
<img src="/images/logopic/logopic_comp.png"
     alt="Research overview"
     style="width:270px; max-width:100%; height:auto;">
</div>

</div>

</div>


## Research areas

<div style="background:#fbfaf6; border:1px solid #c9c9c1; margin:25px 0;">

<div style="padding:25px 30px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid #dddcd5;">
<h2 style="margin:0; font-size:22px; font-weight:400; color:#704568;">
01 &nbsp; Computational X-ray Spectroscopy
</h2>
</div>

<div style="display:flex; gap:35px; align-items:center; padding:25px 30px 30px;">

<div style="flex:1.7;">

<p style="margin-top:0;">
We use multiconfigurational quantum chemical methods for simulating X-ray absorption and emission spectroscopies, enabling direct comparison with high-resolution experiments like resonant inelastic X-ray scattering.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Selected publications</strong>
</p>

<p>
Coming soon.
</p>
</div>

<div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
<img src="/images/Xray.png"
     alt="X-ray spectroscopy"
     style="width:420px; max-width:100%; height:auto;">
</div>

</div>
</div>


<div style="background:#fbfaf6; border:1px solid #c9c9c1; margin:25px 0;">

<div style="padding:25px 30px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid #dddcd5;">
<h2 style="margin:0; font-size:22px; font-weight:400; color:#704568;">
02 &nbsp; Electronic Structure and Chemical Bonding
</h2>
</div>

<div style="display:flex; gap:35px; align-items:center; padding:25px 30px 30px;">

<div style="flex:1.7;">

<p style="margin-top:0;">
We use correlated electronic structure and density functional theory methods to investigate the nature of bonding across the lanthanide and actinide series.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Selected publications</strong>
</p>

<p>
<a href="https://chemrxiv.org/doi/abs/10.26434/chemrxiv.15004087"><em>ChemRxiv</em></a>, 2026.<br>
<a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/jacs.5c20785"><em>Journal of the American Chemical Society</em></a>, <strong>2026</strong>, <em>148</em>, 11758–11768.<br>
<a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.inorgchem.4c04503"><em>Inorganic Chemistry</em></a>, <strong>2025</strong>, <em>64</em>, 242–254.<br>
<a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/jacs.3c12719"><em>Journal of the American Chemical Society</em></a>, <strong>2024</strong>, <em>146</em>, 4098–4111.
</p>

</div>

<div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
<img src="/images/texa_TOC.png"
     alt="Electronic structure"
     style="width:420px; max-width:100%; height:auto;">
</div>

</div>
</div>


<div style="background:#fbfaf6; border:1px solid #c9c9c1; margin:25px 0 45px;">

<div style="padding:25px 30px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid #dddcd5;">
<h2 style="margin:0; font-size:22px; font-weight:400; color:#704568;">
03 &nbsp; Magnetism of f-Element Complexes
</h2>
</div>

<div style="display:flex; gap:35px; align-items:center; padding:25px 30px 30px;">

<div style="flex:1.7;">

<p style="margin-top:0;">
We combine electronic structure theory with experiment to understand magnetic anisotropy and magnetic relaxation mechanisms of f-element systems.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Selected publications</strong>
</p>

<p>
<a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/jacs.5c13255"><em>Journal of the American Chemical Society</em></a>, <strong>2026</strong>, <em>148</em>, 2942–2953.<br>
<a href="https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.inorgchem.6c01375"><em>Inorganic Chemistry</em></a>, <strong>2026</strong>, <em>65</em>, 12541–12556.<br>
<a href="https://doi.org/10.1039/D3SC06175B"><em>Chemical Science</em></a>, <strong>2024</strong>, <em>15</em>, 3003–3010.
</p>

</div>
